From ea9ea70ab014dc5d30a8d0850cf5a15e31a53aed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 06:24:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] hw/display/reims-vgpu-shim: reach guest RAM only, the
 page walk included

Reims calls read_gpa, write_gpa and read_kva from its drain worker, and
now from vCPUs running the iosfc window without the BQL, while holding
its device lock. An access in there that reached a device would take
the BQL in prepare_mmio_access: device lock, then BQL, while the main
loop takes the BQL, then the device lock. Guest addresses Reims follows
can be stale or corrupt, so that cycle is reachable.

MemTxAttrs.memory did not close it. It still let a write through to
read-only RAM and any access through to a RAM device, both of which
are then dispatched; it is checked a piece at a time, so a write that
ran from RAM into a device wrote the RAM half before failing; and the
ld/st helpers a page-table walk uses never look at it, so read_kva's
walk dispatched a table read that hit a device even though its final
read was checked.

Copy guest memory through reims_vgpu_ram_copy() instead
(include/hw/display/reims-vgpu-ram.h). Every piece of the range must be
RAM the CPU could access directly, writable for a write; a range that
wraps is refused; the whole range is checked against one flat view
before any byte moves; a refusal returns an error with nothing copied,
never a zero-filled success. Writes mark the bytes dirty as
address_space_write() did.

And add a no-dispatch section to the memory API: between
memory_no_dispatch_begin() and memory_no_dispatch_end(), an access that
would be dispatched to a device fails with MEMTX_ACCESS_ERROR before the
BQL is taken, in the read and write paths and in the ld/st helpers.
read_kva runs its translation inside one, so a table read that would
reach a device fails the walk, on any target.

tests/unit/test-reims-vgpu-ram covers the copy: RAM across two pieces,
a device refused with the buffer untouched, a write running into a
device refused before any byte is written, read-only RAM, wrapping and
empty ranges, and a worker holding the device lock while the main loop
holds the BQL and waits for it.

